",,True,-1,"/- `H.conjugate x` is the conjugate of a subgroup `sub` by an element `x`. -/
/- - If `sub` is a subgroup and `x` is an element, then `H.conjugate x sub` is also a subgroup. -/
/- - The conjugate of `sub` by `x` is `x * sub * x⁻¹`.-/
/- - `H.conjugate x` is a group if `sub` is a subgroup and `x` is an element.-/
/- - `1` is in `H.conjugate x` if and only if `1` is in `H`.-/
/- - If `h` is in `H`, then `x * h * x⁻¹` is in `H.conjugate x`..-/
/- - If `y * h * x⁻¹` is in `H.conjugate x`, then `h * x⁻¹` is in `sub`. -/
/- - `H.conjugate x` is the only subgroup satisfying `x * sub * x⁻¹`. -/
/- - `H.conjugate x` is a normal subgroup if and only if `x * H * x⁻¹ = H`. -/
/- - `H.conjugate x` acts freely on the left of `H`.-/
