",,True,-1,"-- t1 is a filter
-- t2 is a filter containing t1
-- t3 is the filter of cofinite sets
-- t4 is the filter of sets whose elements are above a finite number
-- t5 is the filter of sets where each element is matched to an index
-- t6 is the filter of sets where all elements are above an index

-- For each t, show that it satisfies the filter properties.
-- E.g. for t1: {s : Set ℕ | ∃ x, s = ↦ x }
--      a) ∀ s ∈ t1, ∃ x, s = ↦ x
--      b) ∩ t1, as a finite intersection of elements of t1, is in t1.
--      c) ∀ s ∃ t ∈ t1 (t ⊂ s). E.g. t = ↦ min s

-- For t2: {s : Set ℕ | ∃ a, ∀ b, a ≤ b → b ∈ s }
--      a) ∀ s ∈ t2, ∃ a, ∀ b, a ≤ b → b ∈ s
--      b) ∩ t2, as a finite intersection of elements of t2, is in t2.
--      c) ∀ s ∃ t ∈ t2 (t ⊂ s). E.g. t = max s

-- For t3, t4, t5, t6: filter_of_hasBasis (something) where each filter has its own basis.
-- E.g. t5: { s : Set ℕ | ∃ f : ℕ → ℕ, ∀ n, n ∈ s ∃ k, f k ∈ s ∧ f k ≤ n }
