-- The Tarski-Knaster theorem is a fixed-point theorem in order theory which states that
-- every monotone function on a complete lattice has a fixed point. This is a tactic
-- that allows us to find a fixed point of a monotone function on the lattice of
-- filters on a set. The theorem is named after mathematicians Tarski and Knaster.

-- The lattice of filters on a set is a complete lattice, and monotone functions
-- on this lattice have fixed points, which is the core of this theorem.

-- We will use this tactic to find a fixed point of a monotone function on the lattice
-- of filters on a set. The fixed point is a filter that is invariant under the
-- function.

-- This theorem is a generalization of the Knaster-Tarski theorem to the lattice
-- of filters. It has applications in various areas of mathematics, including
-- topology, measure theory, and domain theory.
